<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reliance on mercenaries</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reliance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> is a recurring structural feature of empires that hire foreign or professional soldiers instead of relying on citizen or subject levies. Mercenaries can provide skilled forces quickly but are costly and may mutiny or change sides when pay fails. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> all depended heavily on hired troops.</p></div>
